{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_index_landing_page", "label": "grat landing page", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/index.html", "source_location": "lines 1-331", "source_url": "https://grat.layered.work/", "captured_at": null, "author": "phranck", "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_index_structured_data", "label": "SoftwareApplication JSON-LD block", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/index.html", "source_location": "lines 34-51", "source_url": "https://grat.layered.work/", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every value in the structured data also stands in the page, so the block describes the page rather than adding claims a reader cannot see."}, {"id": "docs_index_stack_table", "label": "Stack to grat.config command table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/index.html", "source_location": "lines 164-181", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "grat is tied to no language, framework or package manager: the command runs through /bin/sh from the project root in a session of its own, and the port arrives in PORT."}, {"id": "docs_index_process_tree_boundary", "label": "Following the port up the process tree", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/index.html", "source_location": "lines 188-191", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "grat follows the port back to the process holding it and up its chain of parents. Where that chain does not lead to the command grat started, the service never becomes ready, which rules out anything whose port is held by a separate daemon such as a container started through Docker."}, {"id": "docs_index_ready_means_ready", "label": "Ready means ready, not started", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/index.html", "source_location": "lines 202-222", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A process that has been launched is not a service that answers, so grat waits for a listener owned by the command it started and then for the health path to return before calling it ready."}, {"id": "docs_index_port_lanes", "label": "Port lane diagram", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/index.html", "source_location": "lines 224-254", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ports stop being a thing the developer remembers: the role decides the range and grat allocates inside it across every project it knows about."}, {"id": "docs_index_nav_toggle", "label": "Collapsing section navigation", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/index.html", "source_location": "lines 269-291", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The button states its own condition through aria-expanded and the panel's own height carries the motion, so nothing else has to be moved by hand. Escape closes the panel and returns focus to the button."}, {"id": "docs_index_smooth_scroll", "label": "In-page smooth scrolling", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/index.html", "source_location": "lines 293-319", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The scroll takes a time the page decides rather than one the distance decides, and anything asking for reduced motion gets none at all."}, {"id": "docs_index_copy_button", "label": "Copy-to-clipboard command buttons", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/index.html", "source_location": "lines 321-327", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_index_landing_page", "target": "readme_grat", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/index.html", "source_location": "lines 88, 104, 262-263", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_index_landing_page", "target": "docs_index_structured_data